  "goodToKnow": "Norddeutsch means North German, from Hamburg, Bremen, Schleswig-Holstein, Lower Saxony and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. North Germans are stereotyped as reserved and dry-humoured; the greeting is Moin (or Moin Moin), at any time of day. Low German (Plattdeutsch) is still spoken by some. The north is often said to speak the clearest High German, especially around Hanover. Opposite: süddeutsch."
